      "runtimeObservation": "X-Metaplate-Runtime is \"deno:\": the Deno global exists in Netlify's edge runtime, but Deno.version.deno is an empty string there",
      "cpuLimit": "Netlify documents 50 ms of CPU per request (https://docs.netlify.com/build/edge-functions/limits/); every observed render, including the first requests after each deploy, returned 200, so the limit did not block them. CPU time per request was not measured",
      "caveat": {
        "observed": "2026-11-01, deploy 6ae7a0b5dd9e780c65a1acf3 (the edge site's first deploy, same fixture sources)",
        "symptom": "/og-edge/hosted and /og-edge/edge returned 200 image/png 1200x630, but both were the same solid #064e3b card with no text: identical ETag (062b3cea...c478) and image entropy 0.000. verify-url's format, dimension, and content-type checks alone would have accepted them. The CDN cached both for 24h under Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, so those slugs are not used as evidence.",
        "cause": "Fixture layout, not the runtime. The card was width 100% and height 100% with padding 64 and alignItems flex-end. Satori sizes boxes as content-box, so the card was 1328x758 and its content ended at y=694 on a 630px canvas. A title that fits on one line (\"hosted · metaplate/edge on Netlify Edge\", \"edge · ...\") was drawn entirely below the canvas, leaving the solid background. Longer titles wrap to two lines and the upper line lands on the canvas, which is why cert-990d8a and cert-d16553 rendered text. Reproduced locally on demand with satori 0.63.2, @resvg/resvg-js 2.6.2, and the fixture's exact style: hosted and edge render a 4418-byte single-colour PNG, while cert-990d8a and cert-d16553 render 19767 and 19452 bytes, matching the certified responses byte for byte.",
        "withdrawnDiagnosis": "The original record attributed the blank cards to a first-deploy propagation race on the same-origin font fetch. That was wrong: every asset fetch returned the right bytes because nothing was failing, and the cold-start slugs that rendered text were long enough to wrap.",
        "resolution": "The fixture now sets boxSizing: \"border-box\" (commit c5d9f005703cf1ba1e14c96ebeede0446950df54). Deploy 6ae7ee5478780e9836d6fa03 serves it; the one-line titles e1 and bx-short render text, verified below. The decoded-content check stays on every hosted certification."
      },
